Z||000000||beer_stud_21||09-08-2001||03:22 AM||||Hey all.. I got a quick question that I cant find an answer for in the archives.  I recently got my fiero running and going down the road for the first time.  Now that I got it running and the cat removed (it was all rusted out) I'm trying to fix the small(er) problems before I sell it to my friend in preperation for my move to the mainland.  My problem is this:  My auto tranny is very hard to shift.  The button will depress, but it literally takes both hands to shift from park.  Or to/from any gear for that matter.  The tranny has fluid, and once I get it in gear the car goes down the road fine.  I've only driven the fiero twice, so I dont really know how the auto normally feels, and my tach is broken, so I dont know the exact RPM it shifts at.  But basically I think its all working fine except for just being hard to shift between gears.  Is there any adjustments I dont know about?  The car has been sitting for about 2-2 1/2 yrs so that might have something to do with it.  <P>thanks for any help.<P>-Marlin<BR>85GT/auto/71k miles.<BR>"Marla" -because she needs a good wash and a case worker!..hehe||||reg||1
